  "result": "Done! I've implemented payment tracking:\n\n**Updated src/errors.js:**\n- Added NOT_ISSUED \u2014 \"Invoice must be issued or partially paid to record a payment\"\n- Added OVERPAYMENT \u2014 \"Payment exceeds the amount still owed\"\n\n**Created src/payments.js:**\n- `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })` \u2014 records a payment on an issued/partially_paid invoice\n  - Validates amount is positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID)\n  - Checks for overpayment (OVERPAYMENT)\n  - Only allowed on issued/partially_paid invoices (NOT_ISSUED)\n  - Creates payments array if missing\n  - Updates status automatically:\n    - 'paid' when balance due reaches 0\n    - 'partially_paid' while something is owed\n  - Never mutates input\n- `balanceDue(invoice)` \u2014 returns amount still owed (total - payments)\n\n**Tests:**\n- Created test/payments.test.js with 16 comprehensive test cases covering:\n  - Recording single and multiple payments\n  - Automatic status transitions\n  - Validation of amount (type, sign, no overpayment)\n  - Draft invoice rejection\n  - Balance calculations through payment lifecycle\n  - Non-mutation of input\n- All 137 tests pass\n\n**Design:**\n- Payments stored as array of `{ amount, date }` objects on invoice\n- Balance due calculated as invoice total minus sum of all payments\n- Can record payments multiple times on partially_paid invoices\n- Full payment automatically marks invoice as 'paid'",
